      "description": "US prosecutors unveiled sweeping new criminal charges against former Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro on Thursday, accusing him and his wife of heading a state-sponsored system of repression responsible for beating, asphyxiating, and delivering electric shocks to scores of victims, including several Americans.\nThe torture charges add to pressure on the ousted authoritarian leader and his wife, Cilia Flores, who were seized from their Caracas home by the US military in January to face drug trafficking charges in New York.\nThe updated indictment \"alleges conduct that is truly unthinkable,\" US Attorney Jamie McDonald said outside the Manhattan courthouse where the case is being handled. \"This is the epitome of corruption.\"\nMaduro denies the charges and \"looks forward to his day in court,\" lawyer Barry Pollack said. Flores' attorney said he hadn't yet had time to review the new allegations.\nThe indictment claims Maduro suggested torture methods, sought and received updates on specif",
